# Wiki Curator — Audit Trail

Every automated run of `@wiki-curator` (Mode A and Mode B) and every `/specflow:wiki-init` invocation appends an entry here. The log is append-only and grep-parseable; it is the only persistent record of what the curator has done.

## Format

```markdown
## [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <run-type> — <subject> — wrote <K> / proposed <P>
- Wrote: <path> — <one-line description>
- Proposed (deferred by owner): <path> — <reason>
- Confidence changes: <file> <from>→<to> (<promotion|demotion>)
- Watchlist: <pattern slug> — <consumer count>
```

Run types:

- `wiki-init` — bootstrap, repair, or schema-bump from `/specflow:wiki-init`.
- `mode-A` — per-cycle distillation from the TDD orchestrator (e.g. `triad.md` Phase 8.5).
- `mode-B` — end-of-sprint compilation pass from `/specflow:wiki`.

Subject is whichever of these is most informative:

- For `wiki-init` — the schema version (`schema v1`).
- For `mode-A` — the cycle issue ID (`issue #142`).
- For `mode-B` — the sprint identifier or date range (`sprint-22` or `2026-05-03..2026-05-10`).

## Why this file matters

Three reasons:

1. **Drift detection.** If `git log -- docs/wiki/wiki/_log.md | tail -1` shows the last entry was 60+ days ago, the wiki is almost certainly stale even if the rest of the tree looks fresh. `_hot.md` reads this signal on every Mode B refresh.
2. **Debuggability.** When a curated page reads strangely, grep this file for the run that wrote it. Cross-reference with the source artefact named in the entry.
3. **Confidence trend.** Aggregate `confidence changes` across runs to detect files that bounce between levels — a signal that the underlying decision is unstable, not just the documentation.

## Hard rules

- **Append-only.** Never edit historical entries. Corrections go in a new entry that references the original by timestamp.
- **Always log on Pass 2 success.** No silent applies.
- **Log even on no-op runs** when the run was a deliberate compilation pass (Mode B). For Mode A or `wiki-init`, a true no-op (nothing changed) is logged as a single line: `- No changes; checklist clean.`

